{"type":"message","id":"ceb00ad1","parentId":"932eed3c","timestamp":"2026-02-18T16:55:11.555Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! The write tool works. So the directory exists and is accessible. The issue with exec commands might be that they're not producing output for some reason, but that doesn't matter - I can still work with the filesystem using read, write, edit tools.\n\nNow I need to create the slide generation script. Since there's no existing slide-gen tool, I'll create a Node.js script that uses pdf-lib to generate a 5-slide PDF about \"OpenClaw Features\" with vibrant colors.\n\nLet me:\n1. Create the AgentHr/slide-gen directory if needed\n2. Create a Node.js script that generates the slides\n3. Run it to produce the PDF\n\nI'll need to check if Node.js and npm are available, but I can try to create a simple script and see if pdf-lib can be used. Since I'm in an environment that might have Node.js, I'll create a script that uses pdf-lib to draw slides.\n\nThe slides should cover:\n- Slide 1: Title - OpenClaw Features\n- Slide 2: What is OpenClaw? (brief intro)\n- Slide 3: Key Feature 1 - Comprehensive Toolset\n- Slide 4: Key Feature 2 - Smart Automation\n- Slide 5: Key Feature 3 - Security & Privacy (maybe)\n\nOr some other features. Let me think about what OpenClaw features would be appropriate based on the context.\n\nFrom the AGENTS.md, I see OpenClaw seems to be a framework for building AI assistants with various tools, channels, workflows, etc. So features could include:\n1. Multi-channel support (Discord, WhatsApp, etc.)\n2. Tool integration (browser control, camera, file operations, etc.)\n3. Memory and continuity\n4. Security and privacy controls\n5. Customizable and extensible\n\nLet me proceed to create the script. I'll use pdf-lib which is a Node.js library for PDF manipulation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Good! The write tool works. Now I'll create a slide generation script using pdf-lib. Let me create the necessary directory structure and a script to generate the vibrant 5-slide PDF."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ee66aa3bd95f4f9d90e7aee5","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"// Slide generation script using pdf-lib\nconst { PDFDocument, rgb, StandardFonts } = require('pdf-lib');\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nasync function createOpenClawSlides() {\n  // Create PDF document\n  const pdfDoc = await PDFDocument.create();\n  \n  // Define vibrant colors\n  const colors = {\n    primary: rgb(0.12, 0.34, 0.56), // Deep blue\n    accent: rgb(0.95, 0.45, 0.18), // Vibrant orange\n    secondary: rgb(0.22, 0.62, 0.38), // Green\n    highlight: rgb(0.85, 0.27, 0.27), // Red\n    background: rgb(0.95, 0.95, 0.97), // Light gray\n    text: rgb(0.15, 0.15, 0.18), // Dark gray\n    title: rgb(0.08, 0.16, 0.28) // Navy\n  };\n  \n  // Get fonts (will embed them)\n  const boldFont = await pdfDoc.embedFont(StandardFonts.HelveticaBold);\n  const regularFont = await pdfDoc.embedFont(StandardFonts.Helvetica);\n  \n  // Slide dimensions (16:9 aspect ratio for modern displays)\n  const slideWidth = 800;\n  const slideHeight = 450;\n  \n  // Helper function to create a slide page\n  function createSlide(drawContent) {\n    const page = pdfDoc.addPage([slideWidth, slideHeight]);\n    \n    // Background with gradient effect (simple solid with rounded accents)\n    page.drawRectangle({\n      x: 0,\n      y: 0,\n      width: slideWidth,\n      height: slideHeight,\n      color: colors.background,\n    });\n    \n    // Add decorative elements\n    page.drawRectangle({\n      x: 0,\n      y: slideHeight - 60,\n      width: slideWidth,\n      height: 60,\n      color: colors.primary,\n    });\n    \n    // Draw content\n    drawContent(page, boldFont, regularFont, colors);\n    \n    return page;\n  }\n  \n  // Slide 1: Title\n  createSlide((page, boldFont, regularFont, colors) => {\n    // Title\n    const title = \"OpenClaw Features\";\n    const titleSize = 48;\n    const titleWidth = boldFont.widthOfTextAtSize(title, titleSize);\n    page.drawText(title, {\n      x: (slideWidth - titleWidth) / 2,\n      y: slideHeight - 120,\n      size: titleSize,\n      font: boldFont,\n      color: colors.title,\n    });\n    \n    // Subtitle\n    const subtitle = \"The Ultimate Assistant Framework\";\n    const subtitleSize = 24;\n    const subtitleWidth = regularFont.widthOfTextAtSize(subtitle, subtitleSize);\n    page.drawText(subtitle, {\n      x: (slideWidth - subtitleWidth) / 2,\n      y: slideHeight - 180,\n      size: subtitleSize,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.text,\n    });\n    \n    // Decorative elements\n    page.drawCircle({\n      x: 120,\n      y: slideHeight - 150,\n      size: 20,\n      color: colors.accent,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawCircle({\n      x: slideWidth - 120,\n      y: slideHeight - 150,\n      size: 20,\n      color: colors.secondary,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawCircle({\n      x: slideWidth / 2,\n      y: slideHeight - 240,\n      size: 40,\n      color: colors.highlight,\n    });\n  });\n  \n  // Slide 2: Multi-Channel Support\n  createSlide((page, boldFont, regularFont, colors) => {\n    page.drawText(\"Multi-Channel Support\", {\n      x: 60,\n      y: slideHeight - 80,\n      size: 36,\n      font: boldFont,\n      color: colors.primary,\n    });\n    \n    const channelIcons = [\n      { emoji: \"💬\", text: \"Discord\" },\n      { emoji: \"📱\", text: \"WhatsApp\" },\n      { emoji: \"📧\", text: \"Email\" },\n      { emoji: \"🌐\", text: \"Web\" },\n      { emoji: \"🔔\", text: \"Custom\" }\n    ];\n    \n    let x = 80;\n    let y = slideHeight - 200;\n    channelIcons.forEach((channel, index) => {\n      page.drawText(`${channel.emoji} ${channel.text}`, {\n        x: x + (index % 3) * 200,\n        y: y - Math.floor(index / 3) * 60,\n        size: 28,\n        font: regularFont,\n        color: colors.text,\n      });\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"Seamless integration across multiple platforms\", {\n      x: 60,\n      y: slideHeight - 300,\n      size: 20,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.secondary,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"One assistant, everywhere your users are\", {\n      x: 60,\n      y: slideHeight - 340,\n      size: 20,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.secondary,\n    });\n  });\n  \n  // Slide 3: Powerful Tool Ecosystem\n  createSlide((page, boldFont, regularFont, colors) => {\n    page.drawText(\"Powerful Tool Ecosystem\", {\n      x: 60,\n      y: slideHeight - 80,\n      size: 36,\n      font: boldFont,\n      color: colors.primary,\n    });\n    \n    const tools = [\n      { icon: \"🔍\", name: \"Browser Control\", desc: \"Web automation & extraction\" },\n      { icon: \"📷\", name: \"Camera Access\", desc: \"Visual capture & analysis\" },\n      { icon: \"📁\", name: \"File Operations\", desc: \"Read, write, organize\" },\n      { icon: \"🔌\", name: \"API Integration\", desc: \"Connect any service\" },\n      { icon: \"⚙️\", name: \"Shell Access\", desc: \"System automation\" }\n    ];\n    \n    let y = slideHeight - 180;\n    tools.forEach((tool, index) => {\n      page.drawText(`${tool.icon} ${tool.name}`, {\n        x: 80,\n        y: y - index * 70,\n        size: 24,\n        font: boldFont,\n        color: colors.accent,\n      });\n      \n      page.drawText(tool.desc, {\n        x: 100,\n        y: y - index * 70 - 28,\n        size: 16,\n        font: regularFont,\n        color: colors.text,\n      });\n    });\n  });\n  \n  // Slide 4: Smart Memory & Context\n  createSlide((page, boldFont, regularFont, colors) => {\n    page.drawText(\"Smart Memory & Context\", {\n      x: 60,\n      y: slideHeight - 80,\n      size: 36,\n      font: boldFont,\n      color: colors.primary,\n    });\n    \n    const features = [\n      \"📝 Daily logs & long-term memory\",\n      \"🔄 Continuous context across sessions\", \n      \"⏰ Heartbeat monitoring for proactive help\",\n      \"🗂️ Organized knowledge retention\",\n      \"🔒 Secure, private user data\"\n    ];\n    \n    let y = slideHeight - 180;\n    features.forEach((feature, index) => {\n      page.drawText(feature, {\n        x: 80,\n        y: y - index * 50,\n        size: 22,\n        font: regularFont,\n        color: colors.text,\n      });\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"Your assistant remembers what matters\", {\n      x: 60,\n      y: slideHeight - 320,\n      size: 20,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.secondary,\n      renderToOptionalContentGroup: { name: \"quote\" }\n    });\n  });\n  \n  // Slide 5: Security & Extensibility\n  createSlide((page, boldFont, regularFont, colors) => {\n    page.drawText(\"Security & Extensibility\", {\n      x: 60,\n      y: slideHeight - 80,\n      size: 36,\n      font: boldFont,\n      color: colors.primary,\n    });\n    \n    // Security section\n    page.drawText(\"🔒 Security First\", {\n      x: 80,\n      y: slideHeight - 150,\n      size: 26,\n      font: boldFont,\n      color: colors.highlight,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"• Data privacy & encryption\", {\n      x: 100,\n      y: slideHeight - 190,\n      size: 18,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.text,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"• Controlled external access\", {\n      x: 100,\n      y: slideHeight - 220,\n      size: 18,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.text,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"• Audit trails & permissions\", {\n      x: 100,\n      y: slideHeight - 250,\n      size: 18,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.text,\n    });\n    \n    // Extensibility section\n    page.drawText(\"🔧 Extensible Architecture\", {\n      x: 80,\n      y: slideHeight - 300,\n      size: 26,\n      font: boldFont,\n      color: colors.secondary,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"• Custom skill development\", {\n      x: 100,\n      y: slideHeight - 340,\n      size: 18,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.text,\n    });\n    \n    page.drawText(\"• Plugin system & APIs\", {\n      x: 100,\n      y: slideHeight - 370,\n      size: 18,\n      font: regularFont,\n      color: colors.text,\n    });\n  });\n  \n  // Ensure output directory exists\n  const outputDir = path.join(__dirname, 'AgentHr', 'slide-gen');\n  if (!fs.existsSync(outputDir)) {\n    fs.mkdirSync(outputDir, { recursive: true });\n  }\n  \n  // Save the PDF\n  const outputPath = path.join(outputDir, 'demo-slides.pdf');\n  const pdfBytes = await pdfDoc.save();\n  fs.writeFileSync(outputPath, pdfBytes);\n  \n  console.log(`Slide deck generated successfully at: ${outputPath}`);\n  return outputPath;\n}\n\n// Run the function\ncreateOpenClawSlides()\n  .then(path => {\n    console.log(\"SUCCESS:\", path);\n    process.exit(0);\n  })\n  .catch(err => {\n    console.error(\"ERROR:\", err);\n    process.exit(1);\n  });","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\generate-slides.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":16160,"output":3308,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19468,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771433689581}}
